{
  "about": [
    "Signed GPT-Video webhooks, valid and invalid, that every GPT-Video SDK must verify the same way. Generated: do not edit.",
    "secrets holds standard base64 without the whsec_ prefix: the secret a receiver holds is secretPrefix followed by it. secretNames lists the secrets of the receiver (several during a rotation on its side); when secretText is not null, it is the whole secret instead.",
    "The body is body (text), bodyBase64 (bytes that are not UTF-8, passed as bytes) or bodyParsed (an object, which must be refused). A case with body runs twice: with the text, and with its UTF-8 bytes.",
    "headers are passed as they are: names in any case, values that are a string or a list of strings. A list of signature values is one list of signatures.",
    "nowSec is the current time in seconds; toleranceSec is null for the default, defaultToleranceSec. The tolerance compares whole seconds: the current time rounded down to the second, against the timestamp, in both directions.",
    "expect is the answer: ok with the id and timestamp, or the reason of the refusal.",
    "reference is the answer of the GPT-Video server's own reference check, or null when it cannot take that input. Whatever it accepts, an SDK accepts; an SDK also accepts a missing = padding, unused base64 bits, header names in any case, header values as lists, and its own tolerance."
  ],
  "secretPrefix": "whsec_",
  "defaultToleranceSec": 300,
